{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2140-09-15 00:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Ms. ___. I'm Dr. ___, one of the neurology team doctors. I understand you've been having severe headaches again. Can you tell me what brought you in today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2140-09-15 00:25:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, doctor. The headache came back—bifrontal, pounding, with light and sound sensitivity. I had just gotten better after the last hospital stay, but now it's worse than before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2140-09-15 00:26:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you mentioned photophobia and phonophobia, but no vision changes, numbness, or weakness?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2140-09-15 00:27:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right. No vision loss or numbness. Just one moment of 'brain fog' where I felt unsteady, but no dizziness or falling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2140-09-15 00:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, that’s important. Given your history of pseudotumor cerebri and migraines, we need to check your intracranial pressure. We’ll do a lumbar puncture today to measure that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2140-09-15 00:29:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it hurt? I’ve had one before, but I’m nervous."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2140-09-15 00:30:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll use numbing medicine, and you’ll feel pressure more than pain. It’s important to know your opening pressure—it helps us decide the next steps, especially about your shunt."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2140-09-15 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We just completed the lumbar puncture. Your opening pressure was 30 cm H2O, which is high. That confirms increased intracranial pressure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2140-09-15 12:01:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So that means the shunt might be needed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2140-09-15 12:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Dr. ___ from neurosurgery reviewed your case. Given the high pressure and your ongoing symptoms, they recommend a ventriculoperitoneal (VP) shunt to help drain the excess fluid."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2140-09-15 12:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been back and forth on this. Is it safe? What are the risks?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2140-09-15 12:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a common procedure for your condition. Risks include infection or bleeding, but they’re low. The benefit is long-term control of your pressure and headaches. We’ll schedule it as soon as possible."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2140-09-15 12:06:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I trust you. When will it happen?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2140-09-15 12:07:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning for the day after tomorrow—so Wednesday. In the meantime, we’re adjusting your medications to better control your migraines."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2140-09-15 12:08:25",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What changes are you making?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2140-09-15 12:09:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re restarting amitriptyline at night—it helps with both headaches and sleep. And we’re increasing your Depakote to twice daily instead of once. That’s for migraine prevention."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2140-09-15 12:10:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember Depakote helped before. And what about pain now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2140-09-15 12:11:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "For breakthrough pain, we’ll keep Epidrin as needed, but we’re adding oxycodone for severe episodes—just for short-term use while we get things under control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2140-09-15 12:12:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t like opioids, but if it helps, okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2140-09-15 12:13:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll use it sparingly. Also, your diabetes—we consulted endocrinology. We’re starting Lantus insulin at bedtime for better glucose control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2140-09-15 12:14:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m already on glyburide. Is this because my sugars were high?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2140-09-15 12:15:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your glucose was 269 on admission. Insulin will help stabilize it, especially with the stress of your headaches."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2140-09-16 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We reviewed your chest X-ray yesterday—it was stable, no issues. That clears you for surgery tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2140-09-16 08:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I was worried something would delay the shunt."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2140-09-16 08:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Everything looks good. Your labs are stable too. The team is confident you’re ready for the procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2140-09-17 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, we’re about to take you to surgery. The VP shunt placement is scheduled for 8 AM. Any last questions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2140-09-17 07:01:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just—will I feel better right away?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2140-09-17 07:02:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Some patients feel relief quickly, others take a few days. We’ll monitor your symptoms closely after. The goal is long-term improvement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2140-09-17 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The shunt was placed successfully—no complications. You did great. We’ll keep you overnight for observation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2140-09-17 12:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. My head still hurts, but maybe a little less?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2140-09-17 12:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a good sign. It may take time for the pressure to fully normalize. We’ll keep your pain managed and check a follow-up CT tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2140-09-18 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. The head CT shows the shunt is in the right place. There’s a small amount of air, which is expected, and no bleeding or swelling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2140-09-18 08:01:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So everything’s working?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2140-09-18 08:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The hardware is correctly placed. Now we watch how you feel. Your headache is improving, which is promising."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2140-09-18 08:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m feeling more like myself. Less pressure in my head."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2140-09-18 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow. You’ll go home with updated medications and close follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2140-09-18 08:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What meds will I be on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2140-09-18 08:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Depakote twice daily, amitriptyline at night, your usual blood pressure and diabetes meds, and Lantus insulin at bedtime. For pain, oxycodone as needed—only 15 doses."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2140-09-18 08:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the shunt—what signs should I watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2140-09-18 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call us if you have fever, redness along the shunt path, confusion, or worsening headache. Otherwise, follow up with Dr. ___ in one week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2140-09-19 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re clearing you for discharge. Your neurologic exam is stable, and you’re walking independently."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2140-09-19 08:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready to go home. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2140-09-19 08:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Remember: take your meds as prescribed, monitor your symptoms, and keep your follow-up appointments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2140-09-19 08:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And if the headache comes back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2140-09-19 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Use the oxycodone as directed, but call us if it’s not helping. We may need to adjust the shunt later, but for now, rest and recover."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2140-09-19 08:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my diabetes—should I check my sugars more often?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2140-09-19 08:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, check fasting and bedtime sugars. We’ll review them at your follow-up. Call if they’re consistently high or low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2140-09-19 08:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I feel hopeful this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2140-09-19 08:09:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re hopeful too. The shunt gives us a better way to manage your pressure long-term. Take care, and we’ll see you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2140-09-19 08:10:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. I really appreciate it."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2140-09-15 00:24:00",
    "admission_end": "2140-09-19 14:20:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of idiopathic intracranial hypertension and migraines was admitted for intractable headaches. Her lumbar puncture revealed an elevated opening pressure of 30 cm H2O, leading to the decision for ventriculoperitoneal shunt placement, which was performed successfully on 2140-09-17. During the hospitalization, her migraine prophylaxis was optimized with increased valproic acid and restart of amitriptyline, and her diabetes management was intensified with the addition of Lantus insulin. She showed clinical improvement post-shunt, with reduced headache severity, and was discharged home with close neurology follow-up and updated medication instructions.",
    "problems": [
      "Benign intracranial hypertension",
      "Papilledema associated with increased intracranial pressure",
      "Migraine, unspecified, with intractable migraine, so stated, without mention of status migrainosus",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Other chronic pulmonary heart diseases",
      "Other diseases of lung, not elsewhere classified",
      "Tobacco use disorder",
      "Other acquired absence of organ",
      "Acquired absence of both cervix and uterus",
      "Personal history of urinary calculi",
      "Long-term (current) use of aspirin",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin"
    ]
  }
}
